        "content": "### `UseTools.php`\nAdds the configured tools to the agent’s existing tools. No concrete bug was identified. One point to confirm: duplicate-tool behavior depends on `Tools::merge()`—whether it replaces, rejects, or preserves duplicates.\n\n### `UseFileTools.php`\nRegisters read, write, and edit tools using the configured base directory. The main security consideration is whether those tools prevent path traversal and symlink escapes; this capability alone does not show that protection. It also accepts `baseDir` without validation or normalization, which may make invalid or relative paths behave unexpectedly.\n\n### `UseSelfCritique.php`\nRegisters a self-critique hook after each step. Potential concerns: `maxIterations` accepts zero or negative values, and repeated configuration could add duplicate hooks if registration does not deduplicate them. Neither is necessarily a bug if the hook validates the limit and repeated configuration is not expected.",
